## 6. OneLake Changes the Data Strategy

Mirroring becomes even more interesting when viewed in the context of **OneLake**.

OneLake provides a unified data foundation for Microsoft Fabric.

Instead of every analytics workload maintaining an isolated copy of the same business data, Fabric is designed around a common data layer that can be consumed by multiple analytical experiences.

This enables a broader pattern:

**Operational Data**

↓

**OneLake**

↓

**BI + Engineering + Data Science + AI**

The value is not simply centralized storage.

The real advantage is the ability for multiple analytical workloads to operate around the same organizational data foundation.

